Z||000000||beachbomb||12-17-2000||05:57 PM||||How do i replace the clutch pedal, some-one had a web site that explained how to do it but i lost it, any help?..plmk, thanks..jim(2 '84 Indy's)||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||12-17-2000||06:00 PM||||Jim, it;s really not as hard as it seems. I did it to mine right before the meeting where we met.<P>There is a long bolt that goes through the clutch pedal and brake pedal, remove the nut on one end of the bolt and slide the bolt out enough to remove the pedal. The worst part is spending that much time on your back reaching up under the dash.<P>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||12-17-2000||06:19 PM||||i did mine not too long ago.. biggest pain in the ass is that spring.. i ended up buying a mini hacksaw to saw thru it .. other then that' it's pretty easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">www.v8archie.com has some instructions, that's what i used<P><BR>John<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||12-17-2000||07:16 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch6.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||12-17-2000||10:04 PM||||Thank all, thats exactly what i was looking for <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">///Jim||||reg||6
Z||000005||JohnnyK||12-17-2000||11:11 PM||||Next to the spring, the biggest pain is sliding that long nut out. Didn't budge for me.||||reg||1
